WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.560
There's a
monitor lizard right there,

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:10.880
right on that termite mound,
just basking in the sun.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:19.040
They can either play
dead or they can run
like grease lightning.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:24.080
Let me see if I can
get a better look at it.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.280
I can see that this
monitor could use a little help.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.040
It's actually kind of
good that I found you because

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.680
I'll be real gentle.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:33.960
Oh, yeah, you're
grabbing a hold.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.480
You are starting to wake up.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:36.520
But here's what I want to do.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:37.720
See all these.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:40.040
Look at these horrible ticks.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:44.000
They get these parasites on them
and they just suck their blood.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:50.320
Let's make your day so
much better by getting rid of

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:52.960
some of these nasty parasites.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:56.680
Nobody likes ticks,
including myself.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.480
Monitors have powerful jaws
that can crush bones and even

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:06.040
through hard shells of turtles.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:08.480
And have special
toxins in their saliva that

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:11.320
stops blood from coagulating.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:13.240
This is just a baby.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.760
They can get pretty easily,

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:16.760
six feet long.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.360
So, they're the
biggest lizard in Africa and

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:22.000
they can defend
themselves with those big,

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:25.040
sharp claws with a
very powerful bite.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:29.320
You can see those big
claws built for climbing trees,

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:33.040
built for climbing termite
mounds and built for grabbing

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:36.080
a hold of the ground
when it's in a dead sprint.

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:40.000
They have a forked tongue
that's a lot like a snake, uh.

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.240
They can sort of
smell or sense the air.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:47.720
Well, this was a really,
really lucky find.

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:51.480
But I'm just going to let
you go right where I found you.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:54.960
(grunts)

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:56.640
Pretty smart lizard.

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:58.600
Cool.

